  "caveats": [
    "Single-run measurements on one Apple M5 Max host; they are not a median, confidence interval, or cross-platform performance claim.",
    "S, M, L, XL-single, and PATH-HEAVY are generated fixtures. REAL was not measured because no project-derived capture was available; only fuzz-corpus test fixtures were present.",
    "No explicit cache control was applied, and measurements were run in a fixed tool order, so operating-system cache state and machine load may affect cross-tool comparisons.",
    "Benchmark command exit status and resource use were measured; outputs were not compared pairwise. Semantic coverage is checked by the golden, oracle, and lcov differential suites.",
    "Sorted regular input shards use the direct single-threaded path. M job-setting runs therefore record timing variation, not external-sort worker scaling.",
    "lcov exited with an error on PATH-HEAVY after 89.383 s and used 7,037,177,760 B peak RSS; no throughput is reported for that failed run.",
    "lcov-result-merger PATH-HEAVY reached the 1,800 s timeout. /usr/bin/time did not report RSS on forced termination; a one-second sample during the final 308.3 s observed 841,888 KiB, which is not a full-run peak.",
    "The external Bazel issue evidence is context and was not measured with these commands."
  ]
